13,696 turns.  It played out about the same as the last game, except no early 
speed boots, but two mid-game (around turn 7000) wishes.  At least as many 
stupid mistakes.

As usual I played a neutral Monk and spent my first wish on the Eye.  Why 
Monks?  They are the second-best spellcasters in the game (priests have better 
mana reserves but can't get to Basic in matter spells).  Monks are one of only 
three classes that start with speed, although four more classes get it 
quickly.  Of those six classes, Archeologists have a poor early game and the 
rest have a poor late game (read: they are mediocre spellcasters).

-  Didn't have as many markers as I'd like, so I skipped genociding ;
-  Relatively low HP (227); I didn't have many polyfodder potions.
-  Took 4 tries to get the helm of brilliance to +5.  The extra point is 
important for power regeneration.
-  Conflict took forever to show up on the polypile.  Very annoying. 
-  Mistake: reverse genocided tengu twice to get tele-control
-  Mistake: on the way up with the amulet, stepped in my own hole on a no-tele 
level and had to repeat the level.  The hole was right next to the stairs...

970 creatures vanquished.  Dropped all my non-worn items on the altar to 
decrease score. 

